.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_GET_GROUP_NAME 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_get_group_name
.Nd get group name of a key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_get_group_name
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "char *gname"
.Fa "size_t gname_sz"
.Fa "size_t *gname_len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_group_name
fills in the group name of the
.Fa pkey
into
.Fa gname ,
up to at most
.Fa gname_sz
bytes including the ending NUL byte and assigns
.Em *gname_len
the actual length of the name not including the NUL byte, if
.Fa pkey Ns 's
key type supports it.
.Fa gname
as well as
.Fa gname_len
may individually be NULL, and won't be filled in or assigned in that
case.
.Sh NOTES
Among the standard OpenSSL key types, this is only supported for DH, EC
and SM2 keys.
Other providers may support this for additional key types.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get_group_name
returns 1 if the group name could be filled in, otherwise 0.
.Sh HISTORY
This function was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
